"{\"frames\":[{\"name\":\"08 Coverage and audit\",\"id\":\"306:11359\",\"w\":1800,\"h\":6906,\"text\":\"ACCS / Brand & product system ¶ PROPOSED · v0.1 · OCT 2026 ¶ 08 ¶ COVERAGE AND AUDIT / PROPOSED REFERENCE ¶ Coverage is not approval. ¶ An editable evidence ledger for the ACCS 2026 proposed system. Asset counts distinguish entries from component nodes; visual coverage does not establish working behavior, institutional approval or policy enforcement. ¶ Scope / only page 270:2 modified ¶ Second independent completion audit · 19 Oct 2026. Only page 270:2 is edited. Current eight boards and native values were inspected anew. Corrections affect identity minimum-size wording, semantic bindings/contrast, native focus and targets, legacy mobile type, inherited responsive instances and this evidence ledger. All four protected pages remain read-only. ¶ Requirement ¶ Verified asset or location ¶ Status ¶ Remaining review ¶ Source preservation + proposed logo ¶ 01 Identity · 290:3 Original linked-C direction clearly PROPOSED; five prior logo proposals remain unselected. ¶ PRESERVED / PROPOSED ¶ Institutional logo approval pending. Source colors remain #032E87, #172033 and #FFFFFF. No proposed identity choice is presented as final. ¶ Source colors, extensions + aliases ¶ 02 Color and type · 290:127 02.5 Secondary and accent · 306:39 ¶ NATIVE / PROPOSED ¶ #032E87 / #172033 / #FFFFFF preserved. Teal and purple have seven primitive steps and seven semantic roles each; neither means permission or confidentiality. Institutional color approval pending. ¶ Full 11-style typography system ¶ 02.4 Typography as infrastructure ACCS 2026 text styles ¶ NATIVE / PROPOSED ¶ Display 36/44; H1 30/38; H2 24/32; H3 20/28; H4 16/24; Body large 16/26; Body 14/22; Body small 13/20; Label 14/20; Caption 12/16; Code 13/20. Jakarta / Inter / JetBrains Mono. Mobile H1 uses H2, not a duplicate style. Typography approval pending. ¶ Spacing, radius, elevation, grids + responsive behavior ¶ 03 Foundations · 290:557 03.1–03.5 spatial and interaction rules 07 Responsive layouts ¶ NATIVE GRIDS / PROPOSED ¶ 12 measured app frames at exact widths 1440 / 768 / 390 / 360. Native grids: 12 / 8 / 4 / 4 columns; gutters 24 / 24 / 16 / 16; margins 48 / 24 / 16 / 16. Auto-layout and FILL/HUG rules are attached. Toggle Layout grids to inspect guides. Browser reflow and zoom tests remain required. ¶ Native icon geometry ¶ 03.6 Native icons · 306:296 Search, Menu, Chevron, Bell, Calendar, Forum, Report, Shield, Check, Alert, Close, User ¶ 12 FAMILIES / 36 NODES ¶ 12 Assets entries × Size 16/20/24. Round strokes 1.5/1.75/2px. Icons are not touch targets; mobile wrappers are 44px+. Shield indicates a privacy topic, not a guarantee. ¶ Button states and error placement ¶ 04.1 Actions Primary 299:15 · Secondary 299:22 Tertiary 299:29 · Destructive 299:36 ¶ 4 SETS × 6 STATES ¶ Default / Hover / Pressed / Focus / Disabled / Loading. Error button: N/A; persistent adjacent alerts carry errors. Review source-blue actions and disabled report gating in 07. ¶ Text field coverage ¶ 04.9 Native control states Text field set · 306:523 ¶ 7 STATES ¶ Default / Hover / Focus / Pressed / Disabled / Error / Loading. Persistent Label and Value; loading means async validation. Pressed is pointer-down before focus. ¶ Checkbox coverage ¶ 04.9 Native control states Checkbox set · 306:593 ¶ 14 VARIANTS ¶ Selected=False / True × seven states. Loading represents pending preference save, never automatic consent. Notification preference remains optional in 07. ¶ Modal coverage ¶ 04.9 Native control states Modal set · 306:719 ¶ 7 STATES ¶ Hover / Focus / Pressed apply to the primary action, not the dialog surface. Error preserves the draft; Loading is busy feedback. Static states are not implemented behavior. ¶ Other catalog families ¶ 04 Components · 290:811 04.2–04.8 native local asset families ¶ LOCAL ASSETS REUSED ¶ Select, textarea, radio, navigation, announcement, forum, consultation slots, timeline, privacy notice, alerts, toast, table, mobile record, roles, status, severity and data states. No new masters or definitions in 07–08. ¶ Previous desktop / mobile patterns ¶ 05 Product patterns · 290:1290 Community / consultation and report patterns ¶ PRESERVED / READ-ONLY ¶ Existing product content and reviewer/student distinctions are preserved. Bare action links and breadcrumbs now have 44px minimum-height wrappers; legacy mobile H1 uses the documented native H2 24/32 style. New report examples retain Student · own reports only. ¶ Accessibility, content and permissions ¶ 06 Accessibility and content · 290:1740 07 policy notices and task guidance ¶ TARGET / POLICY PENDING ¶ WCAG 2.2 AA target, not certification. No color-only status. No promises of anonymity, security, response time or finality. Backend authorization, keyboard, browser and assistive-technology testing required. ¶ Community responsive examples ¶ 07.1 Community overview Desktop 1440 / Tablet 768 / Mobile 390 / Narrow mobile 360 ¶ 4 COMPLETE SURFACES ¶ Same announcement, recursion thread, Demo learner 04 and 6 SAMPLE replies. College-community public scope; general-post privacy callout. No restricted report content or identity data. ¶ Consultation responsive examples ¶ 07.2 Consultation booking / review Desktop 1440 / Tablet 768 / Mobile 390 / Narrow mobile 360 ¶ 4 COMPLETE SURFACES ¶ October 2026 calendar; Wed 21 Oct; 10:00–10:30 selected local time. Available, booked and unavailable slots; Course planning; online/in-person; notification checkbox; general-context textarea; summary and Review selection. No booking confirmation. ¶ Restricted report responsive examples ¶ 07.3 Restricted report detail Desktop 1440 / Tablet 768 / Mobile 390 / Narrow mobile 360 ¶ 4 COMPLETE SURFACES ¶ Own DEMO-024 draft; General process question; review summary and illustrative timeline. Durable policy notice, disabled submission, separate permission/identity/recipient guidance and safe browser-title note. ¶ 08.2 / Count semantics and native inventory ¶ Before / original inventory ¶ 45 Assets entries ¶ 9 component sets + 36 standal\"},{\"name\":\"07 Responsive layouts\",\"id\":\"306:9835\",\"w\":3278,\"h\":10016,\"text\":\"ACCS / Brand & product system ¶ PROPOSED · v0.1 · OCT 2026 ¶ 07 ¶ RESPONSIVE LAYOUTS / PROPOSED REFERENCE ¶ One task. Every screen size. ¶ Twelve complete, editable surfaces at their actual widths. Community, consultation planning and an own-report draft preserve task order while navigation and columns adapt. All interface choices are PROPOSED / DEMO. ¶ 07 / Responsive contract · full-size, never scaled ¶ 1440: 12 columns / 24 gutter / 48 margin; separate 240px sidebar. 768: 8 columns / 24 gutter / 24 margin; top navigation. 390 and 360: 4 columns / 16 gutter / 16 margin; compact 44px+ menu controls. Screens use exact fixed widths and natural HUG heights; task bodies FILL width, text wraps, safety copy never truncates. Native grid verification is recorded in 08. ¶ 07.1 / Community overview · PROPOSED / DEMO ¶ Student · community access. Public within the proposed college community; no report or identity data. ¶ Desktop 1440 ¶ 12 col · 24px gutter · 48px margin 240px sidebar + main / support columns. Fixed screen width; natural height. ¶ ACCS ¶ Overview ¶ Community ¶ Consultations ¶ My reports ¶ Student ¶ Proposed student access ¶ College workspace ¶ Search community ¶ PROPOSED / DEMO ¶ Student · community access ¶ Your college, connected. ¶ Find a conversation, catch an update or make space for a question. Community content is public within the proposed college community. ¶ Announcement ¶ DEMO ¶ Make room for your next idea ¶ Explore the proposed peer study circle and share a topic you’d like to learn together. ¶ Community desk · illustrative ¶ Read update → ¶ Study together ¶ DEMO ¶ What helped you understand recursion? ¶ Share a useful explanation or ask a follow-up—everyone starts somewhere. ¶ Demo learner 04 · 6 SAMPLE replies · Open discussion ¶ Read the sample replies below ¶ 6 SAMPLE replies ¶ Synthetic conversation · learning examples, not real student posts. ¶ Demo learner 01 · SAMPLE ¶ Drawing each function call helped me see when the stack returns. ¶ Demo learner 02 · SAMPLE ¶ I started with the base case, then tried an input of one. ¶ Demo learner 03 · SAMPLE ¶ Tracing factorial on paper made the repeated step clearer. ¶ Demo learner 04 · SAMPLE ¶ I wrote down what each call returns before reading the next line. ¶ Demo learner 05 · SAMPLE ¶ Comparing a loop with the recursive version helped me connect the ideas. ¶ Demo learner 06 · SAMPLE ¶ Explaining a tiny example to a study partner revealed what I had missed. ¶ Keep posts general ¶ Avoid personal or case details in community posts. Never post names, identifiers or restricted report content. ¶ A question is a good start. ¶ Be kind, explain your thinking and make room for different ways of learning. Share general academic topics, not personal situations. ¶ Community guidelines ¶ Let’s find a time to talk. ¶ Explore a proposed course-planning consultation. Share general context only; a sample selection is not a booked appointment. ¶ Nonsensitive planning · illustrative schedule ¶ Explore consultation ¶ SYNTHETIC CONTENT · STATIC REFERENCE No real student data. Proposed, not approved. ¶ Tablet 768 ¶ 8 col · 24px gutter · 24px margin Sidebar becomes top navigation. Task sections stack without scaling. ¶ ACCS · College workspace ¶ Search community ¶ Community ¶ Consultations ¶ My reports ¶ PROPOSED / DEMO ¶ Student · community access ¶ Your college, connected. ¶ Find a conversation, catch an update or make space for a question. Community content is public within the proposed college community. ¶ Announcement ¶ DEMO ¶ Make room for your next idea ¶ Explore the proposed peer study circle and share a topic you’d like to learn together. ¶ Community desk · illustrative ¶ Read update → ¶ Study together ¶ DEMO ¶ What helped you understand recursion? ¶ Share a useful explanation or ask a follow-up—everyone starts somewhere. ¶ Demo learner 04 · 6 SAMPLE replies · Open discussion ¶ Read the sample replies below ¶ 6 SAMPLE replies ¶ Synthetic conversation · learning examples, not real student posts. ¶ Demo learner 01 · SAMPLE ¶ Drawing each function call helped me see when the stack returns. ¶ Demo learner 02 · SAMPLE ¶ I started with the base case, then tried an input of one. ¶ Demo learner 03 · SAMPLE ¶ Tracing factorial on paper made the repeated step clearer. ¶ Demo learner 04 · SAMPLE ¶ I wrote down what each call returns before reading the next line. ¶ Demo learner 05 · SAMPLE ¶ Comparing a loop with the recursive version helped me connect the ideas. ¶ Demo learner 06 · SAMPLE ¶ Explaining a tiny example to a study partner revealed what I had missed. ¶ Keep posts general ¶ Avoid personal or case details in community posts. Never post names, identifiers or restricted report content. ¶ A question is a good start. ¶ Be kind, explain your thinking and make room for different ways of learning. Share general academic topics, not personal situations. ¶ Community guidelines ¶ Let’s find a time to talk. ¶ Explore a proposed course-planning consultation. Share general context only; a sample selection is not a booked appointment. ¶ Nonsensitive planning · illustrative schedule ¶ Explore consultation ¶ SYNTHETIC CONTENT · STATIC REFERENCE No real student data. Proposed, not approved. ¶ Mobile 390 ¶ 4 col · 16px gutter · 16px margin Single-column task order. Full-width controls, wrapped labels and 44px+ targets. ¶ ACCS ¶ PROPOSED / DEMO ¶ Student · community access ¶ Your college, connected. ¶ Find a conversation, catch an update or make space for a question. Community content is public within the proposed college community. ¶ Announcement ¶ DEMO ¶ Make room for your next idea ¶ Explore the proposed peer study circle and share a topic you’d like to learn together. ¶ Community desk · illustrative ¶ Read update → ¶ Study together ¶ DEMO ¶ What helped you understand recursion? ¶ Share a useful explanation or ask a follow-up—everyone starts somewhere. ¶ Demo learner 04 · 6 SAMPLE replies · Open discussion ¶ Read the sample replies below ¶ 6 SAMPLE re\"},{\"name\":\"01 Identity\",\"id\":\"290:3\",\"w\":1800,\"h\":2599,\"text\":\"ACCS / Brand & product system ¶ PROPOSED · v0.1 · OCT 2026 ¶ 01 ¶ IDENTITY / PROPOSED REFERENCE ¶ Connection, made accessible. ¶ A proposed identity for Access for College of Computer Studies. Professional, trustworthy, modern, accessible and structured. ¶ LINKED-C DIRECTION / PROPOSED ¶ A service identity, not an institutional seal ¶ ACCS ¶ Access for College of Computer Studies ¶ Your Access to the College of Computer Studies ¶ Two open C forms meet through a shared link: a clear entry point to community, consultation and support. Open terminals suggest access; a common horizontal bridge expresses connection without borrowing a seal or the earlier multicolor A proposal. ¶ 01.1 / A flexible signature ¶ Keep symbol, wordmark and expansion as an intentional lockup. ¶ STACKED · NARROW APPLICATIONS ¶ ACCS ¶ Access for College of Computer Studies ¶ ONE COLOR · INK #172033 ¶ ACCS ¶ REVERSED · WHITE ON SOURCE BLUE ¶ ACCS ¶ 01.2 / Space to remain clear ¶ x = the mark’s stem thickness. Keep at least 2x clear on all sides. ¶ Clear space / 2x minimum ¶ 2x ↕ · no content, rules or imagery ¶ ACCS ¶ Access for College of Computer Studies ¶ ← 2x → x = 10px at 88px mark height ¶ Minimum sizes / digital, actual scale ¶ ACCS ¶ Access for College of Computer Studies ¶ Compact symbol + ACCS wordmark shown: 130px minimum. Full horizontal with expansion: 240px; stacked: 160px. Omit the tagline below 480px. All sizes are PROPOSED. ¶ 23 × 16px ¶ 35 × 24px ¶ 46 × 32px ¶ Mark-only minimum: 24 × 16px (rounded width). Use 35 × 24px or larger for primary navigation. Test the 16px-high mark at 1×; increase its size if the bridge or open terminals lose clarity. ¶ 01.3 / Protect recognition ¶ Misuse is shown for instruction only. Never ship these treatments. ¶ × Don’t / Stretch ¶ Keep original proportions. ¶ × Don’t / Low contrast ¶ Use tested foreground/background pairs. ¶ × Don’t / Altered color ¶ Do not recolor with decorative accents. ¶ × Don’t / Added effects ¶ No shadow, glow, outline or bevel. ¶ The brand should feel ¶ Professional, not bureaucratic. Trustworthy, not absolute. Modern, not decorative. Accessible, not exclusive. Structured, not rigid. ¶ Naming and usage ¶ ACCS = Access for College of Computer Studies. Use the full expansion on first mention. Keep the exact tagline; do not imply an official institutional seal or approved endorsement. ¶ Governance / selection remains open ¶ Five existing logo proposals remain unselected. This original linked-C direction is a sixth proposed direction for review, not an approved identity. Review recognition, small-size reproduction and institutional naming before adoption. Source evidence: Assets/Branding contains five proposals; palette frame 217:82 supplies the three authoritative colors. ¶ ACCS · Access for College of Computer Studies · Proposed, not approved ¶ 01 / 06\"},{\"name\":\"02 Color and type\",\"id\":\"290:127\",\"w\":1800,\"h\":7020,\"text\":\"ACCS / Brand & product system ¶ PROPOSED · v0.1 · OCT 2026 ¶ 02 ¶ COLOR AND TYPE / PROPOSED REFERENCE ¶ A precise visual language. ¶ Three authoritative source colors anchor a proposed accessible extension. The semantic contract below replaces the earlier speculative indigo direction; all extensions remain subject to review. ¶ 02.1 / Source palette ¶ Preserved exactly from palette frame 217:82. ¶ Brand / source ¶ #032E87 ¶ Primary identity and light-theme actions ¶ Ink / source ¶ #172033 ¶ Primary text and dark-theme surface ¶ White / source ¶ #FFFFFF ¶ Base surface and reversed identity ¶ 02.2 / Proposed extensions ¶ Named primitives; status is always paired with text or an icon. ¶ Neutral / deliberate steps, not equal interpolation ¶ neutral/0 ¶ #FFFFFF ¶ neutral/50 ¶ #F5F7FB ¶ neutral/100 ¶ #EDF1F7 ¶ neutral/200 ¶ #DCE2EC ¶ neutral/500 ¶ #65718A ¶ neutral/700 ¶ #46516A ¶ neutral/900 ¶ #172033 ¶ neutral/950 ¶ #0B1220 ¶ Success ¶ 50 ¶ #F0FDF4 ¶ 300 ¶ #86EFAC ¶ 700 ¶ #166534 ¶ 950 ¶ #052E16 ¶ Warning ¶ 50 ¶ #FFFBEB ¶ 300 ¶ #FCD34D ¶ 700 ¶ #854D0E ¶ 950 ¶ #451A03 ¶ Danger ¶ 50 ¶ #FEF3F2 ¶ 300 ¶ #FDA29B ¶ 700 ¶ #B42318 ¶ 950 ¶ #55160C ¶ Info ¶ 50 ¶ #EFF4FF ¶ 300 ¶ #97B5FF ¶ 700 ¶ #032E87 ¶ 950 ¶ #011B4F ¶ 02.3 / Semantic contract · LIGHT ↔ DARK ¶ Native LIGHT and DARK semantic variables are bound to specimens. Use purpose, not hex, in product UI. All choices remain PROPOSED. ¶ ACCS 2026 / Semantic · PROPOSED ¶ LIGHT ¶ DARK ¶ color/canvas ¶ #F5F7FB ¶ #0B1220 ¶ color/surface ¶ #FFFFFF ¶ #172033 ¶ color/raised ¶ #FFFFFF ¶ #22304A ¶ color/text-primary ¶ #172033 ¶ #F5F7FB ¶ color/text-secondary ¶ #46516A ¶ #B8C4D9 ¶ color/border-default ¶ #65718A ¶ #7D8DA6 ¶ color/border-strong ¶ #46516A ¶ #B8C4D9 ¶ color/action/default ¶ #032E87 ¶ #97B5FF ¶ color/action/hover ¶ #022568 ¶ #B8CDFF ¶ color/action/pressed ¶ #011B4F ¶ #729AFF ¶ color/on-action ¶ #FFFFFF ¶ #0B1220 ¶ color/focus ¶ #3157D5 ¶ #97B5FF ¶ color/disabled/bg ¶ #EDF1F7 ¶ #22304A ¶ color/disabled/fg ¶ #46516A ¶ #B8C4D9 ¶ color/success/fg ¶ #166534 ¶ #86EFAC ¶ color/success/bg ¶ #F0FDF4 ¶ #052E16 ¶ color/warning/fg ¶ #854D0E ¶ #FCD34D ¶ color/warning/bg ¶ #FFFBEB ¶ #451A03 ¶ color/danger/fg ¶ #B42318 ¶ #FDA29B ¶ color/danger/bg ¶ #FEF3F2 ¶ #55160C ¶ color/info/fg ¶ #032E87 ¶ #97B5FF ¶ color/info/bg ¶ #EFF4FF ¶ #011B4F ¶ Default control boundaries use border-default, not the decorative neutral/200 divider. Disabled controls keep readable labels but are non-interactive. Dark uses lighter blue actions with dark on-action text, not a naive inversion. Raised is distinguished by border and surface tone before shadow. ¶ LIGHT · surface / text-primary / action ¶ A clearer way to connect ¶ Find a community conversation or plan a consultation. ¶ Browse community ¶ Focus: 2px gap + 3px color/focus ring. Test all pairs before release. ¶ DARK · surface / text-primary / action ¶ A clearer way to connect ¶ Find a community conversation or plan a consultation. ¶ Browse community ¶ Not certified. Validate text, UI boundaries and focus on every surface. ¶ Computed spot checks / WCAG relative luminance ¶ LIGHT / primary action ¶ White on #032E87 · 12.04:1 ¶ Secondary #46516A on white · 7.94:1 ¶ Boundary #65718A on white · 4.90:1 ¶ DARK / primary action ¶ #0B1220 on #97B5FF · 9.25:1 ¶ Secondary #B8C4D9 on #172033 · 9.25:1 ¶ Boundary #7D8DA6 on #172033 · 4.83:1 ¶ STATUS / fg on paired bg ¶ Light: success 6.81 · warning 6.61:1 ¶ Light: danger 6.05 · info 10.92:1 ¶ Dark: success 10.62 · warning 10.39:1 ¶ Dark danger 7.18:1; dark info 8.16:1. Light focus #3157D5 on white is 6.08:1. Calculated from the listed hex pairs using WCAG sRGB relative luminance, rounded to two decimals. Spot checks are not certification; test all implemented states and adjacent surfaces. ¶ 02.4 / Typography as infrastructure ¶ Plus Jakarta Sans headings · Inter body · JetBrains Mono code. ¶ type/display ¶ Plus Jakarta Sans · 700 · 36/44 ¶ Your access starts here ¶ type/h1 ¶ Plus Jakarta Sans · 700 · 30/38 ¶ Community overview ¶ type/h2 ¶ Plus Jakarta Sans · 600 · 24/32 ¶ Connect with your college ¶ type/h3 ¶ Plus Jakarta Sans · 600 · 20/28 ¶ Find the right support ¶ type/h4 ¶ Plus Jakarta Sans · 600 · 16/24 ¶ Consultation details ¶ type/body-large ¶ Inter · 400 · 16/26 ¶ Choose a time that works for you. ¶ type/body ¶ Inter · 400 · 14/22 ¶ Availability is illustrative, not a live schedule. ¶ type/body-small ¶ Inter · 400 · 13/20 ¶ Secondary reading text; not an essential mobile label. ¶ type/label ¶ Inter · 600 · 14/20 ¶ Consultation topic ¶ type/caption ¶ Inter · 500 · 12/16 ¶ DEMO · illustrative content only ¶ type/code ¶ JetBrains Mono · 400 · 13/20 ¶ case.id = \\\"DEMO-024\\\"; // no real student data ¶ Usage / type and theme review ¶ Product UI uses 14–16px body text with persistent 14px labels. Mobile H1 steps to 24/32; body stays 16/26 where space allows, captions never replace labels. Limit reading lines to 65–75 characters (about 680px). Preserve user text scaling. Source blue is #032E87; the earlier Moodboard indigo is not authoritative. The computed spot checks do not replace complete theme and state verification before release. ¶ ACCS · Access for College of Computer Studies · Proposed, not approved ¶ 02 / 06 ¶ 02.6 / Control and inverse aliases · PROPOSED ¶ Audit correction: neutral/dark-border is now #7D8DA6 (previously #64748B). It measures 3.92:1 on raised #22304A and 4.83:1 on surface #172033. Decorative border-subtle is not a control boundary. Success/on-inverse adapts the toast glyph to its inverse background. Existing destructive-action aliases are documented here; no duplicate primitives were added. ¶ color/danger/action ¶ #B42318 ¶ #FDA29B ¶ color/danger/action-hover ¶ #9C1F16 ¶ #FEE4E2 ¶ color/danger/action-pressed ¶ #801A13 ¶ #F97066 ¶ color/danger/on-action ¶ #FFFFFF ¶ #0B1220 ¶ color/border-subtle ¶ #DCE2EC ¶ #22304A ¶ color/success/on-inverse ¶ #86EFAC ¶ #166534 ¶ Columns follow the LIGHT / DARK order. border-subtle → neutral/200 / neutral/dark-raised; success/on-inverse \"},{\"name\":\"03 Foundations\",\"id\":\"290:557\",\"w\":1800,\"h\":3269,\"text\":\"ACCS / Brand & product system ¶ PROPOSED · v0.1 · OCT 2026 ¶ 03 ¶ FOUNDATIONS / PROPOSED REFERENCE ¶ Structure before decoration. ¶ A proposed spatial and interaction foundation: an 8px rhythm, deliberate geometry, predictable responsive behavior and focus that is always visible. ¶ 03.1 / An 8px working rhythm ¶ 4px is an optical exception for icon gaps and fine alignment, not a second grid. ¶ space/8 ¶ 8px ¶ space/16 ¶ 16px ¶ space/24 ¶ 24px ¶ space/32 ¶ 32px ¶ space/40 ¶ 40px ¶ space/48 ¶ 48px ¶ space/64 ¶ 64px ¶ space/80 ¶ 80px ¶ space/96 ¶ 96px ¶ 8 / icon-to-label · 16 / control group · 24 / card inset · 32 / section gap · 48–64 / page regions · 80–96 / major documentation rhythm ¶ 03.2 / Geometry and depth ¶ Subtle elevation signals hierarchy, never security or trust. ¶ Radius / controlled softness ¶ radius/0 ¶ radius/4 ¶ radius/6 ¶ radius/8 ¶ radius/12 ¶ 0 / tables · 4 / chips · 6 / controls · 8 / cards · 12 / overlays. Pills are reserved for compact counts, not every surface. ¶ Elevation / restrained and explicit ¶ Flat ¶ Raised ¶ Overlay ¶ elevation/0 · none elevation/1 · 0 2 8 #1720330D elevation/2 · 0 12 32 #1720331F ¶ Dark surfaces use a tone step and border; avoid luminous shadows. ¶ 03.3 / A grid that changes with the task ¶ Content grows naturally. Do not force desktop columns onto mobile. ¶ Desktop / 12 columns ¶ col ¶ col ¶ col ¶ col ¶ col ¶ col ¶ col ¶ col ¶ col ¶ col ¶ col ¶ col ¶ max reading width / 680px ¶ 24px gutters · 32px page margins at 1024+ · 1200px max content. App sidebar: 240px, separate from the content grid. ¶ Mobile / 4 columns ¶ 16px gutter / 16px margin ¶ 320–599px. Use full-width controls and stack content in reading order. ¶ Viewport ¶ Grid & margins ¶ Navigation ¶ Content behavior ¶ 320–599px ¶ 4 col · 16 gutter · 16 margin ¶ 44px menu + compact header ¶ Single column; tables become labeled records ¶ 600–1023px ¶ 8 col · 24 gutter · 24 margin ¶ Collapsible navigation ¶ Two columns only if each remains ≥280px ¶ 1024–1439px ¶ 12 col · 24 gutter · 32 margin ¶ 240px sidebar ¶ Main + supporting column; reading max 680px ¶ 1440px+ ¶ 12 col · 24 gutter · 48 margin ¶ Persistent sidebar ¶ Content max 1200px; do not stretch paragraphs ¶ 03.4 / Icon geometry and labels ¶ Native icon families below: 16 / 20 / 24px canvases · 1.5 / 1.75 / 2px strokes · round caps and joins. ¶ Overview ¶ Forum ¶ Consult ¶ Report ¶ Access ¶ Visibility ¶ Search ¶ Updates ¶ Success ¶ Warning ¶ Menu ¶ Close ¶ Pair unfamiliar icons with visible text. Icon-only actions need an accessible name; tooltips supplement, not replace it. Decorative icons are hidden from assistive technology. Use status glyph + label, never color alone. ¶ 03.5 / Focus, touch and layout anatomy ¶ Proposed interaction contract for keyboard, pointer and touch. ¶ Light / visible keyboard focus ¶ Book a consultation ¶ focus = 3px #3157D5 offset = 2px / white gap ¶ Never remove focus on keyboard input. Focus must not be obscured by sticky chrome. ¶ Dark / semantic focus ¶ Book a consultation ¶ focus = 3px #97B5FF offset = 2px / dark surface gap ¶ Retain the ring on raised and modal surfaces; validate contrast in context. ¶ Anatomy / a predictable stack ¶ Title + contextual metadata ¶ Readable body → supporting guidance ¶ One primary action ¶ 24px inset · 16px gap · 48px control. 24px minimum target; recommend 44px+ on mobile with 8px separation. ¶ Usage / responsive rules ¶ Preserve task order when columns stack. Let cards grow with translated copy and 200% text zoom; support 320px reflow without two-dimensional page scrolling. Truncate only optional metadata, never labels, errors or safety guidance. Motion is optional and reduced-motion aware; state changes must remain understandable without animation. ¶ 03.6 / Native icon components · PROPOSED ¶ 12 native families, each Size=16 / 20 / 24. Strokes 1.5 / 1.75 / 2px; round caps and joins. Optical padding stays inside the canvas. Geometry is editable. Icons are not touch targets: use a 44px+ labeled control on mobile. Shield denotes a privacy topic, not a security or anonymity guarantee. ¶ Search · 16 / 20 / 24 ¶ Menu · 16 / 20 / 24 ¶ Chevron · 16 / 20 / 24 ¶ Bell · 16 / 20 / 24 ¶ Calendar · 16 / 20 / 24 ¶ Forum · 16 / 20 / 24 ¶ Report · 16 / 20 / 24 ¶ Shield · 16 / 20 / 24 ¶ Check · 16 / 20 / 24 ¶ Alert · 16 / 20 / 24 ¶ Close · 16 / 20 / 24 ¶ User · 16 / 20 / 24 ¶ ACCS · Access for College of Computer Studies · Proposed, not approved ¶ 03 / 06\"},{\"name\":\"04 Components\",\"id\":\"290:811\",\"w\":1800,\"h\":12490,\"text\":\"ACCS / Brand & product system ¶ PROPOSED · v0.1 · OCT 2026 ¶ 04 ¶ COMPONENTS / PROPOSED REFERENCE ¶ A catalog built for real tasks. ¶ Native local ACCS 2026 components and state variant sets. Editable labels are exposed as component properties. These proposed specimens are not production implementations. ¶ Catalog usage / state is part of the contract ¶ Use the ACCS 2026 assets from the local Assets panel. Buttons are 48px high; mobile controls retain at least 44px targets. Focus includes a visible outer ring (see Foundations for the 2px offset recipe). Loading prevents repeat activation; disabled controls remain labeled and explain why where the reason is not obvious. ¶ 04.1 / Actions ¶ Read across: state. Read down: intent. Default control size / 48px. ¶ INTENT / STATE ¶ Default ¶ Hover ¶ Pressed ¶ Focus ¶ Disabled ¶ Loading ¶ Primary ¶ Continue ¶ Continue ¶ Continue ¶ Continue ¶ Continue ¶ Loading… ¶ Secondary ¶ Cancel ¶ Cancel ¶ Cancel ¶ Cancel ¶ Cancel ¶ Loading… ¶ Tertiary ¶ Learn more ¶ Learn more ¶ Learn more ¶ Learn more ¶ Learn more ¶ Loading… ¶ Destructive ¶ Remove draft ¶ Remove draft ¶ Remove draft ¶ Remove draft ¶ Remove draft ¶ Loading… ¶ Use one primary action per task region. Reserve destructive intent for actual removal, not ordinary navigation. A destructive confirmation must name the object and explain whether the action is reversible. ¶ 04.2 / Persistent labels and useful errors ¶ Placeholder text never replaces a label. Required fields use text, not an asterisk alone. ¶ Input / Default ¶ Subject ¶ Course planning ¶ Input / Focus ¶ Subject ¶ Course planning ¶ Error / validation unavailable ¶ Subject ¶ Course planning ¶ Couldn’t validate this subject. Try again; your text is kept. ¶ Input / Disabled ¶ Subject ¶ Submission unavailable ¶ Policy scope is not confirmed. ¶ Textarea / Default ¶ How can we help? ¶ Describe the topic you’d like to discuss. Do not include sensitive details here. ¶ General context only; omit personal details. ¶ Select / Closed ¶ Consultation topic ¶ Course planning ¶ Use a native select where possible. Arrow keys move between options; the visible label persists. ¶ Select / Open ¶ Consultation topic ¶ Course planning ¶ Course planning ¶ Learning support ¶ General question ¶ 04.3 / Selection controls ¶ Labels are clickable. Group related choices with a fieldset and legend. ¶ Unchecked ¶ Email updates ¶ Online consultation ¶ Checked ¶ Email updates ¶ Online consultation ¶ Focus ¶ Email updates ¶ Online consultation ¶ Disabled ¶ Email updates ¶ Online consultation ¶ This option is unavailable. ¶ Checkbox: independent multi-select, Space toggles. Radio: one option per named group, arrow keys move and select. Do not use a disabled checkbox to imply privacy consent. ¶ 04.4 / Navigation and role context ¶ A role badge describes permission context; it is not a privacy or status signal. ¶ ACCS ¶ Overview ¶ Community ¶ Consultations ¶ My reports ¶ Student ¶ Own reports only · proposed permission ¶ College workspace ¶ Search community ¶ Tabs / Selected + Default ¶ Overview ¶ Forum ¶ Consultations ¶ Arrow keys within tablist; Tab enters the active panel. Selected state includes an underline and weight change. ¶ ACCS ¶ 44px menu and notifications. Drawer traps focus only when modal; Escape closes and restores the trigger. ¶ Role badges / proposed permission labels ¶ Student · own reports ¶ Assigned reviewer ¶ Community moderator ¶ Assigned cases only ≠ identity hidden. Do not style roles as severity. ¶ 04.5 / Community and consultation ¶ Casual and encouraging in community; empathetic and clear in support. ¶ Announcement ¶ DEMO ¶ Make room for your next idea. ¶ Explore the proposed peer study circle and share a topic you’d like to learn together. ¶ Community desk · illustrative ¶ Read update → ¶ Study together ¶ DEMO ¶ What helped you understand recursion? ¶ A sample community question. Share a useful explanation or ask a follow-up—everyone starts somewhere. ¶ Demo member · 6 sample replies · Open discussion ¶ Join the conversation → ¶ Consultation slots / illustrative availability ¶ 09:00–09:30 ¶ + Available ¶ 09:00–09:30 ¶ + Available ¶ 09:00–09:30 ¶ + Available ¶ 09:00–09:30 ¶ + Available ¶ 09:00–09:30 ¶ + Available ¶ 09:00–09:30 ¶ + Available ¶ Couldn’t check this slot. Try again. ¶ 09:00–09:30 ¶ + Available ¶ Checking availability… ¶ 09:00–09:30 ¶ ✓ Selected ¶ 09:00–09:30 ¶ ✓ Selected ¶ 09:00–09:30 ¶ ✓ Selected ¶ 09:00–09:30 ¶ ✓ Selected ¶ 09:00–09:30 ¶ ✓ Selected ¶ 09:00–09:30 ¶ ✓ Selected ¶ Couldn’t check this slot. Try again. ¶ 09:00–09:30 ¶ ✓ Selected ¶ Checking availability… ¶ 09:00–09:30 ¶ — Booked ¶ 09:00–09:30 ¶ × Unavailable ¶ Use a radio-group selection model for a single appointment. State is written, not color-only. A selected time is not a confirmed booking. ¶ 04.6 / Cases, status and policy ¶ Serious, structured copy. No promised response deadline or unverified anonymity. ¶ Report / case timeline · DEMO-024 ¶ Review scope pending ¶ Assigned reviewer · DEMO ¶ Policy gate remains active. No sensitive submission. ¶ Draft saved locally · DEMO ¶ Student · own report ¶ Illustrative record only; not a submitted case. ¶ Record created · DEMO ¶ Sample event ¶ DEMO-024 · dates and events are illustrative. ¶ Chronological events use a title, actor role and description. Relative times are optional; exact illustrative timestamps belong in the detail view. ¶ Status and severity / separate families ¶ Draft ¶ Review pending ¶ Resolved ¶ Needs information ¶ Low · sample ¶ Moderate · sample ¶ High · sample ¶ Severity is a proposed classification, not an emergency assessment. ¶ Policy confirmation required ¶ Access permission: assigned reviewers only (proposed). Identity visibility: recipients and anonymity behavior are not yet confirmed. These are separate decisions; restricted access does not mean anonymous. Backend enforcement is required. ¶ Sensitive submission is disabled until scope and policy are confirmed. ¶ 04.7 / Feedback and decisions ¶ Alerts per\"},{\"name\":\"05 Product patterns\",\"id\":\"290:1290\",\"w\":1800,\"h\":4838,\"text\":\"ACCS / Brand & product system ¶ PROPOSED · v0.1 · OCT 2026 ¶ 05 ¶ PRODUCT PATTERNS / PROPOSED REFERENCE ¶ One system. Different responsibilities. ¶ Complete proposed web surfaces at useful working sizes: a friendly community and consultation overview, then a deliberately serious restricted report detail. Every record and schedule is illustrative. ¶ 05.1 / Community overview + consultation booking ¶ Desktop 1258px · mobile 390px · same content, same reading order. ¶ ACCS ¶ Overview ¶ Community ¶ Consultations ¶ My reports ¶ Student ¶ Own reports only · proposed permission ¶ College workspace ¶ Search community ¶ Student · community access ¶ DEMO ¶ Your college, connected. ¶ Find a conversation, catch an update or make space for a question. ¶ Overview ¶ Forum ¶ Consultations ¶ Announcement ¶ DEMO ¶ Make room for your next idea. ¶ Explore the proposed peer study circle and share a topic you’d like to learn together. ¶ Community desk · illustrative ¶ Read update → ¶ Study together ¶ DEMO ¶ What helped you understand recursion? ¶ A sample community question. Share a useful explanation or ask a follow-up—everyone starts somewhere. ¶ Demo member · 6 sample replies · Open discussion ¶ Join the conversation → ¶ A good question is a good start. ¶ Keep posts welcoming, relevant and free of personal or sensitive case details. ¶ Community guidelines ¶ Let’s find a time to talk. ¶ Choose a sample time for a general course-planning consultation. ¶ Illustrative schedule ¶ October 2026 · DEMO ¶ M ¶ 19 ¶ T ¶ 20 ¶ W ¶ 21 ¶ T ¶ 22 ¶ F ¶ 23 ¶ Wed 21 Oct · sample local campus time ¶ 09:00 ¶ + Available ¶ 10:00 ¶ ✓ Selected ¶ 11:00 ¶ — Booked ¶ 14:00 ¶ × Unavailable ¶ Topic ¶ Course planning ¶ Review sample selection ¶ No booking is created. Dates, time zone and availability need service confirmation. No response deadline is promised. ¶ Consultation is support, not an urgent-response channel. Service routing and escalation copy require review. ¶ PROPOSED INTERFACE · FICTIONAL CONTENT · NO REAL STUDENT DATA ¶ ACCS ¶ Student · community access ¶ DEMO ¶ Your college, connected. ¶ Find a conversation, catch an update or make space for a question. ¶ Overview ¶ Forum ¶ Consultations ¶ Announcement ¶ DEMO ¶ Make room for your next idea. ¶ Explore the proposed peer study circle and share a topic you’d like to learn together. ¶ Community desk · illustrative ¶ Read update → ¶ Study together ¶ DEMO ¶ What helped you understand recursion? ¶ A sample community question. Share a useful explanation or ask a follow-up—everyone starts somewhere. ¶ Demo member · 6 sample replies · Open discussion ¶ Join the conversation → ¶ Let’s find a time to talk. ¶ Choose a sample time for a general course-planning consultation. ¶ Illustrative schedule ¶ October 2026 · DEMO ¶ M ¶ 19 ¶ T ¶ 20 ¶ W ¶ 21 ¶ T ¶ 22 ¶ F ¶ 23 ¶ Wed 21 Oct · sample local campus time ¶ 09:00 ¶ + Available ¶ 10:00 ¶ ✓ Selected ¶ 11:00 ¶ — Booked ¶ 14:00 ¶ × Unavailable ¶ Topic ¶ Course planning ¶ Review sample selection ¶ No booking is created. Dates, time zone and availability need service confirmation. No response deadline is promised. ¶ Keep community conversations general ¶ Avoid personal or sensitive case details in public posts. Use the report guidance to understand the proposed access rules. ¶ PROPOSED INTERFACE · FICTIONAL CONTENT · NO REAL STUDENT DATA ¶ Community access does not grant report access. Consultation selection is a preview, not a booked appointment. Mobile moves the consultation rail below the feed; all labels, dates and unavailable states remain visible. ¶ 05.2 / Restricted report detail + timeline ¶ Desktop: assigned reviewer view. Mobile: student’s own draft. Both scopes proposed. ¶ College workspace ¶ Search community ¶ ← Assigned cases / DEMO-024 ¶ Report DEMO-024 ¶ Assigned reviewer · assigned cases only ¶ Draft · policy gate ¶ DEMO ¶ You are viewing an illustrative assigned record. Assignment does not grant access to all college reports. ¶ Policy confirmation required ¶ Access permission: assigned reviewers only (proposed). Identity visibility: recipients and anonymity behavior are not yet confirmed. These are separate decisions; restricted access does not mean anonymous. Backend enforcement is required. ¶ Sensitive submission is disabled until scope and policy are confirmed. ¶ Draft summary ¶ General process question · DEMO ¶ This sample asks how a college process is explained. It contains no personal account, real identity or sensitive attachment. No report has been submitted. ¶ Category: General concern · Created: 19 Oct 2026, 09:00 (illustrative) ¶ Activity / illustrative events ¶ Review scope pending ¶ Assigned reviewer · DEMO ¶ Policy gate remains active. No sensitive submission. ¶ Draft saved locally · DEMO ¶ Student · own report ¶ Illustrative record only; not a submitted case. ¶ Record created · DEMO ¶ Sample event ¶ DEMO-024 · dates and events are illustrative. ¶ Reviewer note · unavailable ¶ This example does not accept case details. ¶ Confirm access scope and recipient policy before enabling sensitive fields. ¶ Save note unavailable ¶ Access scope ¶ Assigned reviewer ¶ Proposed: assigned cases only. Access decisions must be enforced by the backend, not by a badge or hidden navigation. ¶ Identity visibility ¶ Recipients, redaction and anonymity behavior remain unconfirmed. Do not infer confidentiality from a restricted view. ¶ Submission remains gated ¶ Do not accept sensitive content until policy scope, consent and exact recipients are reviewed. ¶ Submission unavailable ¶ No response or resolution deadline is promised. ¶ DEMO RECORD · PROPOSED ACCESS RULES · NO REAL STUDENT DATA ¶ ACCS ¶ ← My reports / DEMO-024 ¶ Report DEMO-024 ¶ Student · own reports ¶ Draft · policy gate ¶ DEMO ¶ You are viewing your own illustrative draft. ¶ Policy confirmation required ¶ Access permission: assigned reviewers only (proposed). Identity visibility: recipients and anonymity behavior are not yet confirmed. ¶ Sensitive submission is disabled unt\"},{\"name\":\"06 Accessibility and content\",\"id\":\"290:1740\",\"w\":1800,\"h\":3413,\"text\":\"ACCS / Brand & product system ¶ PROPOSED · v0.1 · OCT 2026 ¶ 06 ¶ ACCESSIBILITY AND CONTENT / PROPOSED REFERENCE ¶ Clarity is a system responsibility. ¶ A proposed WCAG 2.2 AA target, not certification. Accessibility, privacy and institutional review must be demonstrated in the implemented service—not implied by a polished interface. ¶ 06.1 / Release criteria, not decoration ¶ Validate in context with real keyboard, assistive technology and browser zoom testing. ¶ CONTRAST ¶ 4.5:1 ¶ Normal text. 3:1 for large text (≥24px regular or ≥18.66px bold), UI boundaries and meaningful graphical objects. Validate all themes/states. ¶ TARGETS ¶ 24px minimum ¶ WCAG 2.2 AA target-size criterion includes exceptions. Recommend 44px+ mobile targets and 8px separation. Make the visible label clickable. ¶ REFLOW ¶ 320px / 200% ¶ Support a 320 CSS-pixel viewport and 200% text enlargement without clipped labels or lost actions. Avoid two-dimensional page scrolling. ¶ KEYBOARD ¶ Visible focus ¶ Logical DOM order, skip link, unobscured focus, no keyboard traps. Reduced motion removes nonessential movement, never the state signal. ¶ Contrast exceptions for inactive controls do not justify unreadable instructions. Layout should accommodate user text spacing, high contrast and forced-colors modes. Test with keyboard-only use, screen readers, 200–400% browser zoom and reduced-motion settings. ¶ 06.2 / Control-category expectations ¶ Implementation checklist for every candidate family in the catalog. ¶ Control category ¶ Keyboard and focus ¶ Screen reader and content expectations ¶ Buttons & links ¶ Tab reaches each action; Enter activates. Space activates buttons. ¶ Use native semantics, an action-oriented name, and disabled/busy state. Links navigate; buttons act. ¶ Inputs & textarea ¶ Tab in logical order; preserve normal editing keys. ¶ Associate persistent label, hint and error. Announce required/invalid. Error summary links to fields. ¶ Select / combobox ¶ Native select preferred. Arrows choose; Enter confirms; Escape closes. ¶ Announce expanded state, selected value and active option. Do not intercept text editing unexpectedly. ¶ Checkbox & radio ¶ Space toggles checkbox. Arrows move/select radio options. ¶ Use fieldset/legend for groups. Expose checked state; label includes the full choice meaning. ¶ Tabs & navigation ¶ Arrows within tabs; Tab enters panel. Current link stays in sequence. ¶ Label tablist, tab and panel relations. Expose selected tab and current page. Drawer trigger exposes expanded state. ¶ Calendar & slots ¶ Offer keyboard date entry; arrows move within a documented grid. ¶ Announce full date, time zone, availability and selected state. A single slot uses a radio-group model. ¶ Cards, chips & badges ¶ Only actual actions receive focus. Do not make nested actions ambiguous. ¶ Cards have headings; badges are text. Status includes words or symbols, not color alone. ¶ Alerts, errors & toast ¶ Keep focus unless recovery requires deliberate movement. ¶ Polite status for updates; assertive only for urgent errors. Announce once, avoid duplicate live regions. ¶ Modal & popover ¶ Move focus inside modal; contain Tab; Escape closes when allowed. ¶ Dialog has name/description; background is inert. Return focus to trigger. Do not trap focus in nonmodal content. ¶ Tables & mobile records ¶ Native table navigation; sort buttons expose sort state. ¶ Caption, column headers and row relationships. Mobile records retain each field label and reading order. ¶ Empty, loading & error ¶ Keep retry reachable; do not reset the user’s place. ¶ Mark busy region; skeletons are decorative. Show a meaningful empty state and nontechnical recovery action. ¶ Timeline & privacy notice ¶ Events read chronologically; policy text stays reachable. ¶ Use ordered structure, explicit actor roles and dates. Identity visibility is not inferred from permission labels. ¶ Errors and live regions ¶ Explain what went wrong and how to fix it next to the field; retain entered values. On a failed submit, provide a linked error summary and a deliberate focus destination. Distinguish network failure from validation failure. Do not announce every keystroke or skeleton update. Do not expose sensitive details in errors, analytics, URLs or live-region messages. ¶ 06.3 / Permission is not confidentiality ¶ Proposed rules; exact policy and recipients require institutional confirmation. ¶ Role ¶ Permission scope · proposed ¶ Identity / confidentiality ¶ Policy gate ¶ Student ¶ Own report drafts and records ¶ Not confirmed; do not promise anonymity ¶ Confirm recipients, consent and self-access ¶ Assigned reviewer ¶ Assigned cases only ¶ Identity visibility and redaction unconfirmed ¶ Confirm assignment, delegation and audit rules ¶ Community moderator ¶ Moderate community posts ¶ No report access by default ¶ Confirm public-post and moderation rules ¶ Administrator ¶ Manage configuration ¶ No automatic permission to read cases ¶ Explicit authorization required for case access ¶ Do / neutral notification ¶ “There’s an update to a record you can access.” ¶ Route to an authenticated, authorized view. Redact names, case categories, narrative, attachments and sensitive status from email subject lines, push previews and lock screens. ¶ Don’t / expose the record ¶ Do not put an allegation, student identity or report description in a notification. A role label is not permission enforcement. Restricted access is not a guarantee of confidentiality. ¶ 06.4 / Three contexts, one honest voice ¶ Direct language, meaningful actions and no unverified claims. ¶ Community / encouraging ¶ Try: “What helped it click for you? Share an explanation or ask a follow-up.” ¶ Avoid: “Only experts should answer.” ¶ Invite participation; protect people from personal disclosure. ¶ Support / empathetic ¶ Try: “Choose a sample time that works for you. You can review it before continuing.” ¶ Avoid: “We will reply within 24 hours.” ¶ Offer a clear next step without a service-level pr\"}],\"components\":[{\"frame\":\"01 Identity\",\"name\":\"ACCS 2026 / Identity / Logo Horizontal\",\"type\":\"COMPONENT\",\"variants\":[],\"w\":473,\"h\":116,\"radius\":0,\"fills\":[],\"pad\":[0,0,0,0],\"gap\":24},{\"frame\":\"01 Identity\",\"name\":\"ACCS 2026 / Identity / Logo Stacked\",\"type\":\"COMPONENT\",\"variants\":[],\"w\":265,\"h\":208,\"radius\":0,\"fills\":[],\"pad\":[0,0,0,0],\"gap\":16},{\"frame\":\"01 Identity\",\"name\":\"ACCS 2026 / Identity / Logo Compact Minimum\",\"type\":\"COMPONENT\",\"variants\":[],\"w\":130,\"h\":35,\"radius\":0,\"fills\":[],\"pad\":[0,0,0,0],\"gap\":8},{\"frame\":\"03 Foundations\",\"name\":\"ACCS 2026 / Icon / Search\",\"type\":\"COMPONENT_SET\",\"variants\":[\"Size=16\",\"Size=20\",\"Size=24\"],\"w\":16,\"h\":16,\"radius\":0,\"fills\":[],\"pad\":[0,0,0,0],\"gap\":0},{\"frame\":\"03 Foundations\",\"name\":\"ACCS 2026 / Icon / Menu\",\"type\":\"COMPONENT_SET\",\"variants\":[\"Size=16\",\"Size=20\",\"Size=24\"],\"w\":16,\"h\":16,\"radius\":0,\"fills\":[],\"pad\":[0,0,0,0],\"gap\":0},{\"frame\":\"03 Foundations\",\"name\":\"ACCS 2026 / Icon / Chevron\",\"type\":\"COMPONENT_SET\",\"variants\":[\"Size=16\",\"Size=20\",\"Size=24\"],\"w\":16,\"h\":16,\"radius\":0,\"fills\":[],\"pad\":[0,0,0,0],\"gap\":0},{\"frame\":\"03 Foundations\",\"name\":\"ACCS 2026 / Icon / Bell\",\"type\":\"COMPONENT_SET\",\"variants\":[\"Size=16\",\"Size=20\",\"Size=24\"],\"w\":16,\"h\":16,\"radius\":0,\"fills\":[],\"pad\":[0,0,0,0],\"gap\":0},{\"frame\":\"03 Foundations\",\"name\":\"ACCS 2026 / Icon / Calendar\",\"type\":\"COMPONENT_SET\",\"variants\":[\"Size=16\",\"Size=20\",\"Size=24\"],\"w\":16,\"h\":16,\"radius\":0,\"fills\":[],\"pad\":[0,0,0,0],\"gap\":0},{\"frame\":\"03 Foundations\",\"name\":\"ACCS 2026 / Icon / Forum\",\"type\":\"COMPONENT_SET\",\"variants\":[\"Size=16\",\"Size=20\",\"Size=24\"],\"w\":16,\"h\":16,\"radius\":0,\"fills\":[],\"pad\":[0,0,0,0],\"gap\":0},{\"frame\":\"03 Foundations\",\"name\":\"ACCS 2026 / Icon /